---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import MethodProvenance from "../../components/MethodProvenance.astro";
const defaultCode = `f <- function(x) x^3 - x - 2`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Secant Method — CMNA" description="Watch the secant method use successive chords for arbitrary R functions.">
<header class="page-head"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Root finding · CMNA Laboratory</p><h1 class="page-title">Estimate the slope from the curve itself.</h1><p class="lede">The secant method keeps Newton's x-axis intercept idea but replaces the derivative with a chord through two recent function values.</p></div></header>
<section class="section"><div class="shell two-column"><article class="content"><h2>A derivative made from two points.</h2><p>Two function evaluations define a secant line. Where that line crosses the x-axis becomes the next approximation, and the newest two points define the next secant.</p></article><aside class="callout"><strong>CMNA's seed</strong><p>The package begins with your starting value and a second point displaced by <code>10 * tol</code>, so the tolerance participates in the initial geometry.</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="section lab-section"><div class="shell" data-root-geometry-lab data-method="secant">
<div class="lab-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Bring your own function</p><h2 class="section-title">One R function. No derivative.</h2><p class="lede">Play the successive chords and watch their x-intercepts become new guesses.</p></div><div class="lab-expression"><span>Runtime</span><code data-status>Preparing R…</code></div></div>
<div class="r-guided-grid"><section class="r-guided-editor"><div class="r-editor-label"><span>R</span><small>Define <code>f</code></small></div><textarea class="r-editor r-function-editor" data-r-code spellcheck="false">{defaultCode}</textarea><div class="r-guided-controls"><label>starting x<input type="number" value="1.5" step="any" data-x0 /></label><label>tolerance<input type="number" value="0.000001" min="0" step="any" data-tol /></label></div><div class="r-run-row"><button class="button r-run" type="button" data-run disabled>Run secant in R</button><button class="r-reset" type="button" data-reset>Reset R session</button></div></section>
<aside class="r-guided-primer"><h3>What can go wrong?</h3><p>If the two function values become nearly equal, the secant slope collapses. Try functions and starting values that make the chord almost horizontal.</p></aside></div>
<div class="lab-summary" data-summary></div><div class="lab-plot-frame"><svg class="lab-plot" role="img" aria-label="Secant chord iteration" data-plot></svg></div><div class="lab-stepper"><button class="button secondary-on-light" type="button" data-play disabled>Play convergence</button><label><span data-step-label>Iteration</span><input type="range" min="0" max="1" value="0" data-step disabled /></label></div><p class="lab-status" data-step-detail></p>
<div class="lab-table-wrap"><table class="lab-table"><thead><tr><th>n</th><th>previous x</th><th>current x</th><th>f(current)</th><th>next x</th></tr></thead><tbody data-rows></tbody></table></div>
</div></section><script is:inline type="module" src="/js/root-geometry-lab.js"></script></BaseLayout>
